<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 15:05:46 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Perspective</category><title>Sheer devastation: '80 percent of Gazan infrastructure has been destroyed'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sheer-devastation-80-percent-of-gazan-infrastructure-has-been-destroyed</link><description>
New images posted this week by Google Maps show the utter destruction in Gaza. It's been estimated that 61 tonnes of rubble need to be cleared – that's 20 times the amount of rubble generated in all wars across the world over the last 18 years.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e19ae4d8-bda6-11f1-9f08-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-19057684946abe7242d6e809-56187074.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e19ae4d8-bda6-11f1-9f08-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-19057684946abe7242d6e809-56187074.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8f370bc4-bd6d-11f1-bfd6-d1eca8fc919d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 14:16:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Israel's Netanyahu says co-pilot tried to crash Tel Aviv-bound plane</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261001-israel-s-netanyahu-says-co-pilot-tried-to-crash-tel-aviv-bound-plane</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, October 1: A FlyDubai flight was diverted to Saudi Arabia after the pilot was stabbed by his co-pilot in what the Israeli media are calling a terror attack. The co-pilot was detained by off-duty pilots on board and passengers before making a safe landing in Saudi Arabia. Also in the news, Cornell University's college campus culture is back under scrutiny after a shocking sexual assault claim. Plus, a man learns that Singapore does not take AI slop lightly.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef0e3a14-bd62-11f1-9a20-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-10-01T05-22-59-158Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef0e3a14-bd62-11f1-9a20-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-10-01T05-22-59-158Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">00d3fb94-bd63-11f1-a5e0-6f81c04d46ed</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 10:00:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dheepthika LAURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>FlyDubai cockpit incident turns focus to crew-related hijackings</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-flydubai-cockpit-incident-turns-focus-to-crew-related-hijackings</link><description>
The pilot of the FlyDubai flight is suspected of having stabbed his copilot midflight in an apparent attempt to crash the plane. The incident has turned focus to similar incidents in the past, where deliberate crashes or near crashes have been instigated by on or off-duty crew.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/943c8a4c-bd6b-11f1-8b55-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25311357526495.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/943c8a4c-bd6b-11f1-8b55-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25311357526495.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1377d7c0-bd6d-11f1-a266-d5c188696c63</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 08:01:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/943c8a4c-bd6b-11f1-8b55-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25311357526495.jpg">© Martin Meissner, AP/ Illustration picture</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Live: Pilot wounded in FlyDubai incident is ‘in good health’, Indian embassy in UAE reports</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-live-flydubai-suspends-flights-to-and-from-israel-after-pilot-attack</link><description>
Smit Machchhar, the pilot wounded in a violent altercation in an Israeli-bound passenger jet Wednesday, is “in good health and recovering well”, India’s embassy in the United Arab Emirates said Thursday. Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu earlier alleged the co-pilot believed to have stabbed Machchhar had undergone “Islamist radical indoctrination”, without providing evidence for the claim. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/46c3c9c0-bce8-11f1-8f3e-098db7fa8bc7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273571043073.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/46c3c9c0-bce8-11f1-8f3e-098db7fa8bc7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273571043073.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8f7a3888-bd5c-11f1-9fcf-f76c9a7496bd</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 05:58:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/46c3c9c0-bce8-11f1-8f3e-098db7fa8bc7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273571043073.jpg">© Ariel Schalit, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Like a 'rollercoaster': passengers describe harrowing flydubai flight</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/like-a-rollercoaster-passengers-describe-harrowing-flydubai-flight</link><description>
As flight FZ 1073 from Dubai to Tel Aviv approached the Jordanian border on Wednesday, passengers knew in an instant that something was wrong when the plane began plummeting from the sky in a rapid dive. It was like "we were having very big turbulence, but there was no turbulence", passenger Almog Italie told AFP, describing the sensation of losing thousands of feet of altitude in seconds as similar to riding a "rollercoaster". FRANCE 24's August Hakansson reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/133b75fc-bd16-11f1-b85e-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16771745746abd7f51257970-94832487.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/133b75fc-bd16-11f1-b85e-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16771745746abd7f51257970-94832487.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b6ecf812-bd14-11f1-b6f9-ad25e63e2287</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:31:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘Attempted terror attack’: What happened on board the rerouted Flydubai flight?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-attempted-terror-attack-what-happened-on-board-the-rerouted-flydubai-flight</link><description>
The co-pilot of a flight from Dubai to Tel Aviv ​tried ‌to crash the plane after stabbing the pilot, but passengers then ⁠held him down while other pilots landed the plane safely in Saudi Arabia, Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said ‌on Wednesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b44a2bda-bce6-11f1-9437-098db7fa8bc7/w:1024/p:16x9/mini3-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b44a2bda-bce6-11f1-9437-098db7fa8bc7/w:1024/p:16x9/mini3-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c62e1938-bce6-11f1-a15d-718e41bf9f8a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:04:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Mixed reactions in Iraq on final day of US-led coalition withdrawal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-mixed-reactions-in-iraq-on-final-day-of-us-led-coalition-withdrawal</link><description>
The US military announced on Wednesday that it has completed the withdrawal of all American troops from Iraq, ending a 12-year mission to fight the Islamic State group. The last US troops left an air base in northern Iraq under a deal between Baghdad and Washington. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/69f1cab4-bcc0-11f1-b65a-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-32.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/69f1cab4-bcc0-11f1-b65a-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-32.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">27561aa6-bcc1-11f1-9b55-ab09d4b8b084</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:27:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Netanyahu says Israel is preparing for other ‘potential threats’ after pilot tried to crash plane</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260930-israel-bound-flight-diverted-to-saudi-arabia-after-brawl-between-pilots</link><description>
Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said that one of the pilots of an Israel-bound flight had tried to kill the other and crash the plane, but that passengers and crew had managed to overpower him and safely land the plane in Saudi Arabia. All the passengers have since arrived in Israel, and Saudi authorities have arrested and are interrogating the alleged assailant.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9de8a560-bca5-11f1-b941-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273268796814.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9de8a560-bca5-11f1-b941-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273268796814.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b2e0203c-bca6-11f1-b79e-91afbb6948b5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 08:25:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9de8a560-bca5-11f1-b941-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273268796814.jpg">© Malak Harb, AP file picture</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>US forces leave Iraq, raising fears of Iran-backed militias amid power vacuum</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260930-us-forces-leave-iraq-raising-fears-of-iran-backed-militias-amid-power-vacuum</link><description>
US forces are withdrawing from their remaining bases in Iraq on Wednesday, completing a pullout agreed under former president Joe Biden as fears grow over the security vacuum it could leave. Iraqi officials and analysts warn the departure could embolden Iran-backed militias and give Islamic State group fighters room to rebuild their capabilities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/47df05ee-bcbc-11f1-8052-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/Iraq-4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/47df05ee-bcbc-11f1-8052-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/Iraq-4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d328d1b8-bc6a-11f1-8e74-ff6732142757</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:04:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/47df05ee-bcbc-11f1-8052-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/Iraq-4.jpg">© Ahmad al-Rubaye, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Settler raid on West Bank village injures Israeli forces, drawing rare government rebuke</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260929-settler-raid-on-west-bank-village-injures-israeli-forces-drawing-rare-government-rebuke</link><description>
More than 100 Israeli settlers stormed a village in the occupied West Bank early on Tuesday, setting fire to Palestinian properties and wounding three members of Israel's security forces. The raid, which drew rare government condemnation, came as the military attempted to accompany a Palestinian family back to their home after they had been displaced by earlier settler attacks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d947c52-bbf1-11f1-91bc-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/0118268afa52a94c8110d9ec5c3e1f3d1420de20.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d947c52-bbf1-11f1-91bc-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/0118268afa52a94c8110d9ec5c3e1f3d1420de20.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8e66ce8c-bbf1-11f1-a2c6-21fb1f6856f3</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 10:35:57 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d947c52-bbf1-11f1-91bc-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/0118268afa52a94c8110d9ec5c3e1f3d1420de20.jpg">© Zain Jaafar, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Video shows Iranian police beating, sexually humiliating teenage detainee</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260929-iran-police-video-teenage-detainee-abuse</link><description>
A video posted in mid-September showing Iranian police officers beating and sexually harassing an arrested teenage boy has caused widespread outrage in Iran. Experts say such mistreatment of people accused of common crimes is frequent in Iran, but the footage provides rare visual evidence of what they describe as a recurring practice within the police force.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5a691568-b8ea-11f1-8115-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-09-25-at-4-06-05-PM.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5a691568-b8ea-11f1-8115-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-09-25-at-4-06-05-PM.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">92aee040-bbe4-11f1-8f24-1f6053ff47a2</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 09:56:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5a691568-b8ea-11f1-8115-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-09-25-at-4-06-05-PM.png">© Les Observateurs</source><dc:creator>Ershad ALIJANI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran says it expects US response Tuesday on plan to reopen Strait of Hormuz</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260929-iran-says-expects-us-response-tuesday-plan-reopen-strait-of-hormuz</link><description>
Iran's Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi said Tehran expects Washington to respond to its proposal to reopen the Strait of Hormuz on Tuesday. In exchange for reopening the vital shipping route, Tehran is seeking guarantees including a regional ceasefire, the lifting of sanctions on its oil sector and an end to the US naval blockade.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bcc1d708-bbca-11f1-b635-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26268737302690.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bcc1d708-bbca-11f1-b635-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26268737302690.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eeedbab0-bbcc-11f1-8750-c5eb01e184f1</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:32:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bcc1d708-bbca-11f1-b635-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26268737302690.jpg">© Yuki Iwamura, AP Photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title><![CDATA[Trump 'flips & flops' with Iran between making a deal and threats to attack in ‘devastating fashion’]]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260928-saudis-furious-trump-flips-flops-between-deal-with-iran-and-attacks-in-devastating-fashion</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Barbara Slavin, Distinguished Fellow at the Stimson Center. She describes the US-Iran conflict as a dangerous combination of military escalation, diplomatic ambiguity and political calculation. Slavin sees an absence of true diplomacy: the recent indirect contacts between Washington and Tehran, mediated by Qatar, have been too limited and too fragile to produce any serious breakthrough. For her, this amounts to "kabuki diplomacy": they half engage while positioning themselves against any appearance of compromise.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/770340f4-bc0a-11f1-8dc6-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6026989696abbbe576b3cc4-31536915.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/770340f4-bc0a-11f1-8dc6-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6026989696abbbe576b3cc4-31536915.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d973d0c0-bb68-11f1-8748-9145122832b6</guid><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:18:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Trump expects Iran talks next week after rejecting seven-day truce proposal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260927-trump-expects-iran-talks-next-week-after-rejecting-seven-day-truce-proposal</link><description>
US President Donald Trump on Sunday said he expected talks with Iran to resume next week, despite rejecting Tehran’s proposal for a seven-day truce followed by the reopening of the Strait of Hormuz. Trump raised the possibility of renewed air strikes on Iran but also said he anticipated further negotiations.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4817a61c-ba8a-11f1-b4fe-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/040b658896f965b502ca28b500bf7f44524d2c6c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4817a61c-ba8a-11f1-b4fe-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/040b658896f965b502ca28b500bf7f44524d2c6c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0ef20500-babf-11f1-888a-f742704bf1de</guid><pubDate>Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:10:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4817a61c-ba8a-11f1-b4fe-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/040b658896f965b502ca28b500bf7f44524d2c6c.jpg">© Alex Wroblewski, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel revokes Dutch diplomats' West Bank credentials over settlement goods ban</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260927-israel-revokes-dutch-diplomats-credentials-settlement-sanctions</link><description>
Israel will revoke the diplomatic accreditation of Dutch officials based in the occupied West Bank after the Netherlands began enforcing a ban on goods from Israeli settlements, Foreign Minister Gideon Saar said Sunday. The officials have seven days to surrender their Israeli-issued diplomatic papers, he added.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5cc8df4-b215-11f1-b4b8-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T133257Z-1437535793-RC2OFNA4YO0U-RTRMADP-3-SLOVENIA-ISRAEL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5cc8df4-b215-11f1-b4b8-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T133257Z-1437535793-RC2OFNA4YO0U-RTRMADP-3-SLOVENIA-ISRAEL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c52868a4-babb-11f1-8220-e929450cecca</guid><pubDate>Sun, 27 Sep 2026 21:47:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5cc8df4-b215-11f1-b4b8-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T133257Z-1437535793-RC2OFNA4YO0U-RTRMADP-3-SLOVENIA-ISRAEL.jpg">© Borut Zivulovic, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Middle East: Palestinians plan first local elections in 20 years</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-palestinians-plan-first-local-elections-in-20-years</link><description>
Oliver McTernan, Director and co-founder of Foward Thinking in London, is our guest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d8d6e988-b9a4-11f1-9a48-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-03T112835Z-1925832320-RC2LBNAZ3NGZ-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-SETTLERS-ATTACK-FUNERAL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d8d6e988-b9a4-11f1-9a48-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-03T112835Z-1925832320-RC2LBNAZ3NGZ-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-SETTLERS-ATTACK-FUNERAL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">44d652fc-b9a2-11f1-aa35-7160de579780</guid><pubDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 12:29:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Middle East: An art centre for children in occupied West Bank</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-an-art-centre-for-children-in-occupied-west-bank</link><description>
To help children process their experiences of war, an art center has been established in the West Bank. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f8ff5a2-b982-11f1-8a2e-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260926-080933-081128-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f8ff5a2-b982-11f1-8a2e-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260926-080933-081128-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">94837caa-b982-11f1-967e-4559c82829b4</guid><pubDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 10:10:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Middle East: Iran proposes Hormuz plan, Donald Trump reportedly refuses</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-iran-proposes-hormuz-plan-donald-trump-reportedly-refuses</link><description>
The United States had yet to publicly respond on Saturday after Iran offered a plan to reopen the strategic Strait of Hormuz, though reports indicated that President Donald Trump had rejected the proposal. The waterway key to the world's oil supply is central to the conflict between the US and Iran, which is at a stalemate after nearly seven months, though new mediation efforts took place this week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5c91426e-b982-11f1-a52f-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260926-080640-080800-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5c91426e-b982-11f1-a52f-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260926-080640-080800-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">619238fe-b982-11f1-b946-cf61c9c134fc</guid><pubDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 09:35:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israelis, Palestinians must 'reboot relations': Absence of diplomatic route means 'perpetual war'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israelis-palestinians-must-reboot-relations-absence-of-diplomatic-route-means-perpetual-war</link><description>
Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Yossi Mekelberg, Senior Consulting Fellow of the Middle East and North Africa Programme at Chatham House. Can Israel continue to define its future primarily through security and territorial control? Mekelberg challenges the notion that military operations, incursions and settlement expansion can constitute a sustainable political objective. He identifies a potential transition beyond the Netanyahu era as an opportunity to reconsider the relationship between Israeli and Palestinian societies. His central argument is that the continuation of war without a political endgame risks a state of perpetual conflict.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0018edc8-b97a-11f1-add3-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-210056-211223-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0018edc8-b97a-11f1-add3-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-210056-211223-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">063faad4-b97a-11f1-9f37-b74edc30a206</guid><pubDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 07:50:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Trump rejects Iran’s seven-day plan to reopen Strait of Hormuz</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260926-trump-reportedly-rejects-iran-s-7-day-plan-to-reopen-strait-of-hormuz</link><description>
US President Donald Trump on Saturday rejected an Iranian plan to reopen the Strait of Hormuz. Iran's Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi presented the proposal to Trump’s envoy Steve Witkoff a day earlier on the sidelines of a UN gathering in New York. The plan stipulated that the important waterway would reopen seven days after an agreement was reached.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d59dfb18-b94e-11f1-9c2f-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/de49252b3547da24497242e0261e32a55f43d83e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d59dfb18-b94e-11f1-9c2f-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/de49252b3547da24497242e0261e32a55f43d83e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d682270c-b94e-11f1-9ad4-d72b7ddab526</guid><pubDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 02:06:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d59dfb18-b94e-11f1-9c2f-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/de49252b3547da24497242e0261e32a55f43d83e.jpg">© Charly Triballeau, AFP, File picture</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Yemen's president calls on his people to mobilise against Iran-backed Houthis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260925-yemen-president-calls-on-his-people-to-mobilise-against-iran-backed-houthis</link><description>
Yemen’s Riyadh-based President Rashid al-Alimi on Friday called on ‌his people to mobilise and join the armed ‌forces while offering a general amnesty to the Iran-backed Houthi rebels who have seized swaths of Yemen's Red Sea coast and imposed a naval blockade on Saudi Arabia.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1ad03680-b907-11f1-add1-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-14T132010Z-886379123-RC21JNAQNIP4-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-HOUTHI.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1ad03680-b907-11f1-add1-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-14T132010Z-886379123-RC21JNAQNIP4-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-HOUTHI.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5979e66e-b921-11f1-8fcf-11e0360ada64</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:41:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1ad03680-b907-11f1-add1-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-14T132010Z-886379123-RC21JNAQNIP4-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-HOUTHI.jpg">© Houthi Military Media via Reuters </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>'Iran has dragged us into this conflict,' top Emirati diplomat Anwar Gargash says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260925-iran-has-dragged-us-into-this-conflict-top-emirati-diplomat-anwar-gargash-says</link><description>
